BT /F1 18 Tf 0.13 0.16 0.22 rg 72.0 708.0 Td (Why some PDFs cannot be searched) Tj ET
0.996 0.557 0.078 rg 72 686.0 46 2.5 re f 0 rg
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 652.0 Td (A PDF can store letters in two very different ways. A text layer stores) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 635.0 Td (each character as a character with a font reference -- that is what search) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 618.0 Td (reads. An outlined or scanned page stores shapes: the letters are vector) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 601.0 Td (curves or pixels, and no search engine can find a word in them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 574.0 Td (If a document produces zero results in the search panel, it almost certainly) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 557.0 Td (has no text layer. Standard extraction tools return zero characters for) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 540.0 Td (such files. OCR is the only way to recover searchable text from them -- the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 523.0 Td (letters must be recognized back into characters before they can be indexed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 496.0 Td (The word annotation appears on this page too -- by design.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 469.0 Td (Tip: files exported from design tools with fonts converted to outlines, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 452.0 Td (stamped and flattened through certain pipelines, lose their text layer the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 0.08 0.08 0.1 rg 72.0 435.0 Td (same way a scan does. Rendering still looks perfect; search finds nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 0.45 0.47 0.52 rg 72.0 52.0 Td (Dynamsoft Codepool sample -- page 2 of 3) Tj ET
endstream
